			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Enhance process control and error handling in bootstrap\n\n- Introduce `CocoonExitPreventedError` with exit code tracking to clearly distinguish blocked exit attempts from other errors\n- Increase `Error.stackTraceLimit` to 100 following VS Code extension host practices for deeper debugging visibility\n- Add detailed stack traces to both exit and crash prevention warnings for better diagnostics\n- Improve exit code reporting in log messages and errors to include attempted numeric values\n- Add confirmation logs after critical patches (process.exit/crash) and environment variable setup\n- Strengthen error messages with specific exit codes and standardized formatting\n- Add maintenance TODO regarding Node.js internal API stability for 'natives' module patching\n\nThese changes improve Cocoon's ability to safely host extensions by:\n1. Providing clearer differentiation between allowed/prevented process exits\n2. Aligning debugging capabilities with VS Code extension host expectations\n3. Enabling faster root cause analysis through enriched logging context\n4. Maintaining compatibility with extensions expecting Electron environment signals via ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE",
