			"Message": "feat(Shim/Crypto): expand delegated methods and add stubs for secure operations\n\n- Directly delegate additional Node.js `crypto` methods to native implementation in Cocoon environment:\n  - Add `randomFill`, `randomFillSync`, `pbkdf2`, and `pbkdf2Sync` for broader API compatibility\n  - Simplify `randomBytes` implementation by using native type signatures\n- Implement error-throwing stubs for sensitive operations requiring Mountain coordination:\n  - `generatePrime` and `generateKeyPair` now throw explicit errors indicating need for proxying\n- Maintain direct delegation for common/safe operations like hashing, HMAC, and UUID generation\n\nThis change enhances VS Code extension compatibility by supporting more cryptographic functions while enforcing Land's security model. Sensitive operations requiring system entropy or secure key storage are explicitly blocked until Mountain RPC integration is implemented.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Extensions using `crypto.generatePrime` or `crypto.generateKeyPair` will now receive errors instead of implicit missing method exceptions. Requires coordination with Mountain RPC implementation for full functionality.",
