			"Message": "feat(Shim): Improve command execution error handling and telemetry\n\n- Introduced `CocoonCommandError` class to wrap extension command errors with extension context and original stack traces, enhancing error tracking in the `Cocoon` extension host\n- Added telemetry reporting via `IExtHostTelemetry` for command execution duration, success/failure states, and error reasons using VS Code's `StopWatch` and trusted value patterns\n- Refactored RPC method signatures (`$registerCommand`, `$unregisterCommand`, `$executeCommand`) to use direct parameters instead of argument arrays, aligning with Mountain's `MainThreadCommandsHandler` expectations\n- Implemented argument revival for commands executed via RPC from Mountain to ensure proper type conversion in `Cocoon`\n- Added comprehensive telemetry metadata classifications for performance monitoring and error analysis\n- Improved error logging with extension context and retry handling for Mountain-proxied commands\n\nThese changes strengthen the reliability of cross-process command execution between `Cocoon` and `Mountain`, critical for maintaining VS Code extension compatibility while providing observability into the shim layer's operation. The telemetry integration supports Land's performance optimization goals by identifying slow or failing extension commands.",
